## Problem
`buildTree()` walks all nodes every time, even when only one node changed. For 1700 nodes this is wasteful.

## Current caching (outline.svelte.ts:279-293)
```ts
// Only checks if nodes array reference changed
if (cachedTreeNodes === nodes && ...) {
  return cachedTree;
}
```
This cache is **all-or-nothing** - any node change invalidates the entire tree.

## Proposed: Subtree-level caching
Cache each subtree independently, keyed by:
- Parent ID
- Children's IDs + order
- Relevant node properties (collapsed state)

```ts
// Cache structure
type SubtreeCache = Map<string | null, {
  childIds: string[];        // For invalidation check
  collapsedStates: boolean[];
  result: TreeNode[];
}>;

function buildTree(parentId, depth, ...) {
  const children = childrenOf(parentId);
  const childIds = children.map(c => c.id);
  const collapsedStates = children.map(c => c.collapsed);

  const cached = subtreeCache.get(parentId);
  if (cached && 
      arraysEqual(cached.childIds, childIds) &&
      arraysEqual(cached.collapsedStates, collapsedStates)) {
    return cached.result;
  }

  // Build and cache...
}
```

## Benefits
- Deleting leaf node: only rebuild parent's children list
- Deleting node with siblings: only rebuild that level
- Most subtrees remain cached

## Invalidation strategy
- On any node change, clear cache for affected parent
- On delete: clear cache for deleted node's parent
- On move: clear cache for old parent and new parent

## Complexity
Medium - need to track what changed, not just that something changed

