## Description
Add keyboard shortcut Ctrl+] to zoom into the current node's subtree.

## Behavior
- Ctrl+] on a node with children → zoom to show only that subtree
- Ctrl+[ → zoom out one level (or to root)
- Same as double-click zoom (otl-yap) but via keyboard

## Implementation
Add to OutlineItem.svelte handleKeyDown:
```ts
// Ctrl+] : zoom in
if (event.key === ']' && mod) {
  event.preventDefault();
  outline.zoomTo(nodeId);  // needs to be implemented
  return true;
}

// Ctrl+[ : zoom out
if (event.key === '[' && mod) {
  event.preventDefault();
  outline.zoomOut();  // needs to be implemented
  return true;
}
```

## Related
- otl-yap: Double-click bullet to zoom into subtree (same feature, different trigger)

## Files
- app/src/lib/OutlineItem.svelte (keyboard handler)
- app/src/lib/outline.svelte.ts (add zoomTo/zoomOut methods)

The Svelte `outline.svelte.ts` has a full undo/redo system that is missing from the React store.

## Features
- Undo stack (max 100 entries)
- Redo stack (cleared on new actions)
- Keyboard shortcuts: Ctrl+Z (undo), Ctrl+Y/Ctrl+Shift+Z (redo)

## Undo Entry Structure
```ts
interface UndoEntry {
  description: string;
  undo: UndoAction;
  redo: UndoAction;
  timestamp: number;
}

type UndoAction =
  | { type: 'create'; node: Node }
  | { type: 'delete'; id: string }
  | { type: 'update'; id: string; changes: Partial<Node> }
  | { type: 'move'; id: string; parentId: string | null; position: number }
  | { type: 'swap'; id: string; position: number; otherId: string; otherPosition: number }
```

## Operations that push undo
- addSiblingAfter/Before
- toggleCollapse
- indentNode/outdentNode
- swapWithPrevious/Next
- deleteNode
- toggleCheckbox
- toggleNodeType
- setDate/clearDate
- setRecurrence
- moveNodeTo

## Files
- React store: `app/src/store/outlineStore.ts`
- Svelte source: `app/src/lib/outline.svelte.ts` (lines 63-75, 2131-2241)

Typing `[[` should open a search popup to insert wiki links, but nothing happens.

## Root Cause
The code exists but isn't wired up:
1. `WikiLinkSuggestion.tsx` component exists ✓
2. `createWikiLinkInputHandler` is imported but **never added** to the TipTap editor
3. No state for showing the suggestion popup

## Svelte Implementation (`OutlineItem.svelte`)
```svelte
// State (line 43)
let showWikiLinkSuggestion = $state(false);
let wikiLinkQuery = $state('');
let wikiLinkRange: { from: number; to: number } | null = null;

// Plugin added to editor (line 231)
createWikiLinkInputHandler(
  (query, range) => {
    wikiLinkQuery = query;
    wikiLinkRange = range;
    showWikiLinkSuggestion = true;
  },
  () => {
    showWikiLinkSuggestion = false;
  }
)

// Rendered when active (line 1446-1447)
{#if showWikiLinkSuggestion}
  <WikiLinkSuggestion ... />
{/if}
```

## React Fix Needed (`OutlineItem.tsx`)
1. Add state: `showWikiLinkSuggestion`, `wikiLinkQuery`, `wikiLinkRange`, `wikiLinkPosition`
2. Add `createWikiLinkInputHandler` plugin to TipTap editor extensions
3. Calculate popup position from cursor
4. Render `WikiLinkSuggestion` when `showWikiLinkSuggestion` is true
5. Handle selection: delete range and insert wiki link node

